cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this demonstration site, please cite the CAST methods paper below
  (preferred-citation) and link to this repository. The CAST method is the work
  of Yang et al.; this repository demonstrates it on simulated data and is not
  the analysis code of that paper.
title: "CAST demo website: causal survival trajectories on simulated oncology data"
abstract: >-
  An interactive teaching demo on simulated oncology survival cohorts where the
  true treatment effect is known. It shows how confounding by indication biases a
  naive comparison, how a Causal Survival Forest adjusts for measured
  confounding, where each standard baseline breaks, what an unmeasured confounder
  does to all of them at once, and how CAST extends per-horizon causal estimates
  into a smooth treatment-effect trajectory with a covariance-aware band. No
  patient data are used or distributed.
type: software
